  reportTitle: Mission Report
  intro: Here is how your junior astronaut training mission went.
  sources: 'NASA OSDR study OSD-314: ''Adaptive response of Arabidopsis seedlings in microgravity and Mars reduced gravity environment is enhanced by red light photostimulation'' (Villacampa et al., International Journal of Molecular Sciences, 2021; doi:10.3390/ijms22020899).


    NASA CCMC DONKI documentation for space-weather event types and API terms. DONKI data is research and prototyping quality; NOAA SWPC is the official forecast source.


    NASA Mars Trek (trek.nasa.gov/mars) is the reference for future real map layers. The current landing map is a fictional training map, not Mars Trek data.'
  notNasaNote: This game is a learning simulation, not an official NASA product. Game values, landing sites, and space-weather alerts are invented for play.
  bands:
  - title: Mission Complete
    message: Your crew finished the training mission and brought home a report. Try again to compare choices!
    minimumScience: 0
    color: {r: 0.29, g: 0.79, b: 0.94, a: 1}
  - title: Science Started
    message: You collected useful practice data. Every careful choice adds to the crew's science story.
    minimumScience: 10
    color: {r: 1, g: 0.72, b: 0.16, a: 1}
  - title: Junior Researcher
    message: Excellent work! You compared options, explained your choices, and filled the science log.
    minimumScience: 20
    color: {r: 0.29, g: 0.87, b: 0.5, a: 1}
  replayLabel: Play Again
  menuLabel: Main Menu
